        label: 'Temple \u2014 community resources & what to know',
        items: [
          {title:'Signs your Philadelphia rowhome needs a panel upgrade', sub:'Flickering lights, frequently tripping breakers, or a fuse box instead of a circuit breaker panel are red flags. Most rowhomes built before 1970 were wired for 60-amp service \u2014 modern households need 150\u2013200 amp.', tag:'Guide'},
          {title:'PECO electrical safety resources \u2014 free home energy assessments', sub:'PECO offers free in-home energy assessments for eligible customers. Technicians check wiring safety, identify hazards, and recommend efficiency upgrades. Schedule at peco.com or call 1-800-494-4000.', tag:'Resource'},
          {title:'PA electrical contractor licensing \u2014 what the law requires', sub:'Pennsylvania does not have a statewide electrician license, but Philadelphia L&I requires all electrical contractors to be licensed locally. Always verify the L&I license at phillyinfo.org before work begins.', tag:'Rights'}
