        items: [
          {title:'Philadelphia Architecture Center \u2014 public programs and walking tours', sub:'The Center at 1218 Arch St offers free and low-cost public programs, neighborhood walking tours, and school partnerships exploring Philly\u2019s built environment. Open to all residents.', tag:'Community'},
          {title:'When do you need an architect vs. a designer in Philadelphia?', sub:'Philadelphia L&I requires architect-stamped drawings for structural changes, additions over 500 sq ft, and change-of-use permits. Interior renovations without structural work can often use a designer or design-build contractor.', tag:'Guide'},
