          {title:'Philadelphia Rat Patrol \u2014 free inspections and block-level coordination', sub:'The city\u2019s rat abatement program offers free property inspections, bait station installation, and community cleanup coordination. Request service at phila.gov/rat-patrol or call 311.', tag:'Resource'},
          {title:'What Philadelphia renters can do when landlords ignore pest problems', sub:'Under Philadelphia Housing Code Section 9-3901, landlords are responsible for pest-free conditions. Tenants can report to L&I, who will inspect and issue violations. Document everything in writing first.', tag:'Rights'},
          {title:'Integrated Pest Management for rowhomes \u2014 what actually works', sub:'Sealing gaps around pipes and utility entries, removing standing water, and keeping trash lids sealed reduces rodent entry more effectively than repeated chemical treatments. A licensed IPM professional can assess entry points.', tag:'Guide'}
