        items: [
          {title:'Philadelphia restaurant inspection scores \u2014 how to read them', sub:'The Philadelphia Department of Public Health posts inspection results at phila.gov/foodprotection. Scores are not a simple letter grade; look at the violation categories (critical vs. non-critical) for a full picture.', tag:'Guide'},
          {title:'Philly restaurant weeks and community dining events', sub:'Philadelphia Restaurant Week runs twice yearly (January and September) with fixed-price menus at hundreds of restaurants. The Black Restaurant Week (typically March) spotlights Black-owned dining across the region.', tag:'Community'},
